    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92), representing our strongest starts. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** thrives despite a left-on-left matchup against Abbott because his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in a tight SB race, and the favorable SP_xERA of 4.89 offers a prime opportunity for extra-base hits. Similarly, **Casey Schmitt** benefits from a massive 11% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages against Michael Lorenzen; his ability to capitalize on a favorable park factor and a spot in the #3 hole makes him an essential start. **Kazuma Okamoto** rounds out our top-tier plays (60.22), as he is positioned to feast on the generous 5.58 xERA of Germ\u00e1n M\u00e1rquez, assuming the projected #5 spot holds.\n\nWhile **Yordan Alvarez** (58.65) and **Trea Turner** (56.81) face tough matchups against elite arms like Gore and Skubal, their raw talent keeps them locked in. We are particularly cautious regarding the workload for **Colt Keith** (46.91) and **Chase Meidroth** (44.69); they hover near our marginal threshold, with **Colt Keith** specifically hampered by the high-caliber arsenal of Wheeler and an elite catcher suppressing his SB upside. The most difficult decision at the bench was **Carson Benge** (43.14). He narrowly missed the cut because the projected platoon disadvantage and lower floor relative to the utility versatility of **Junior Caminero** (58.35) made him the odd man out. Investors should monitor the lineup for **Kazuma Okamoto** closely, as any shift from the #5 spot would necessitate a re-evaluation of his current efficiency score.",
